ok - a recovered lease keeps refusing allocation on a treehouse that does not prove persistent recovered leases, names the upgrade, and runs no pool command
ok - neither an unproven nor a proven provider is asked for status to place an unleased slot (the unproven refusal names the upgrade, the proven one the lease remedy)
ok - a capability answer whose holder is the old holder plus a newline, or only a newline, is not proof and cannot make an old-holder slot pass; a distinct protected holder still refuses an old-holder slot, and the guard runs no status and changes no holder
ok - with a proven persistent-recovered-lease capability a recovered slot on the protected holder holding a current copy stays untouched while the spawn takes the free slot, whatever its root's state or state order
ok - a proven capability relaxes only the recovered lease: unleased, missing, and unreadable entries still refuse
ok - an old holder refuses before treehouse get with a named cause and the cutover remedy, and the guard never runs treehouse status, so no holder or lease changes when the consumer is the caller
ok - the shared guard bin/fm-home-seed.sh runs refuses an old recovered holder until the provider's cutover adopts it, changes no holder, and passes beside a protected slot
ok - the spawn's own treehouse get is executed against the private pool with an explicit root, the test reads the slot that command chose, the recovered slot is byte-preserved, and a get that hands out the recovered slot is detected
not ok - old/recovered-first: the provider's cutover did not move the entry to the protected holder
exit=1
